<title>USA: Southwestern Public Service Co Q2 net off.</title>
<headline>Southwestern Public Service Co Q2 net off.</headline>
<dateline>AMARILLO, Texas 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ended Feb 28.</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.19		    $0.41</p>
<p> Net			  7,732		   18,081</p>
<p> Revs		     226,155		  203,785</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  40,918		   40,918</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.29		    $2.83</p>
<p> Net			 93,725		  120,880</p>
<p> Revs		     935,190		  869,760</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  40,918		   40,918</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 Q2 and 12 month periods include a one-time write-off of approximately $16 million, or $0.25 a share, after tax from its investment in BCH waste-to-energy project in North Carolina.</p>
<p>1997 12-month period charge offset by $0.19 a share gain from sale of water rights held by Quixx unit, which invested in BCH.</p>
<p>1997 12-month period includes gains of $0.13 a share from accounting adjustment to delivered-not-billed revenues and a settlement with New Mexico customers of a 1985 wholesale rate case of $0.11 a share.</p>
